    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Moved from v5.19.0 to v5.21.0: engine v5.21.0 makes the installer identity-driven, publishing its own `install.sh` template and `tools/build_installer.py` so a distribution can generate a rebranded installer instead of forking the engine's 1000-odd-line script. This pin now tracks four assets instead of two -- `pegasus` and `build_zipapp.py` as before, plus `build_installer.py` and the `install.sh` template it fills in -- so `tools/build_darq.py` can produce `dist/install.sh` alongside `dist/darq`. All four hashes were downloaded from the published v5.21.0 release assets and hashed independently; they match both the release manifest (commit 4a927766bf0fbe33082fe21092104cfa053b947b) and each asset's own published `.sha256` sidecar."
  }
